{"c":[{"id":"7b00489091032a4a","sum":"A13: the ask field lives in the keyable, non-activating activity list panel, whose sendEvent intercepts Return/Tab/Esc/Cmd-Z (the field editor eats Tab and Esc first). Golden protocol line 32 now has the calendar role (b610800); HelperProtocolTests compares it as is.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T195705Z-0509a06fd894e25f","text":"Caret's ask field lives in the activity list panel (OverlayPanel keyable, non-activating); Return/Tab/Esc are intercepted in the panel's sendEvent, because the field editor eats Tab and Esc before SwiftUI onKeyPress (A13).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T195705Z-b2dcf80bc4cc0ac3","text":"helper/fixtures/golden/protocol.ndjson line 32 still holds the host's pre-calendar default roles; HelperProtocolTests compares it with calendar removed until the screen track rewrites the line (A13).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"028910e321e65bd9","sum":"A13: cua-driver background keys refuse Caret's own panels; drive the ask field with scripts/pid-keys.swift. reader --calendar-test without Calendar access ends the event run as handoff blocked tcc before any calendarGrant, so no revoke to assert.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T195705Z-c193056a6c54a222","text":"cua-driver's background press_key/type_text refuse Caret's own panels (not in the host's AXWindows: off_space_or_ax_unresolved); drive the ask field with apps/caret/scripts/pid-keys.swift (CGEventPostToPid, executable rechecked per event) (A13).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T195705Z-d51a855e42ff6461","text":"With reader --calendar-test on a Mac without Calendar access, the event run ends as handoff blocked tcc at the first calendarFind, before any calendarGrant: no grant is issued, so don't assert a revoke there (A13).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
